<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 11 February, from 660 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">660 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,366 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Legendary founding of Japan by Emperor Jimmu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to the 8th-century chronicles, Jimmu, said to descend from the sun goddess Amaterasu, became Japan's first emperor on this day. The legend is commemorated as National Foundation Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1531 CE <span class="tih-ago">495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English clergy recognise Henry VIII as head of the Church</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under threat of prosecution, the Convocation of Canterbury acknowledged Henry as Supreme Head of the Church in England 'as far as the law of Christ allows'. The full break with Rome followed by 1534.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1752 CE <span class="tih-ago">274 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pennsylvania Hospital, the first in the American colonies, opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Founded by Benjamin Franklin and Dr Thomas Bond, the Pennsylvania Hospital admitted its first patients in Philadelphia. It was the first hospital in what became the United States.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1847 CE <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Edison is born in Milan, Ohio</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edison patented more than 1,000 inventions, including the phonograph and a practical incandescent lamp. His laboratory at Menlo Park pioneered organised industrial research.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1858 CE <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bernadette Soubirous sees her first vision at Lourdes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 14-year-old miller's daughter reported seeing a lady in white in the grotto of Massabielle. Lourdes grew into one of the most visited Catholic pilgrimage sites in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1929 CE <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lateran Treaty creates Vatican City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mussolini's government and the Holy See agreed to recognise Vatican City as an independent state. The treaty ended the 'Roman Question' that had divided Church and Italian state since 1870.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1990 CE <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nelson Mandela walks free after 27 years in prison</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mandela left Victor Verster Prison near Paarl hand in hand with his wife Winnie, watched by millions on television. Four years later he was elected South Africa's first Black president.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
